{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require all Government Ministers to be Elected Members of Parliament",
        "additional_details": "Ministers should be directly accountable to voters through election.\r\nGovernment ministers exercise significant executive power and make decisions affecting the public. Those who hold ministerial office should therefore have a direct democratic mandate from the electorate rather than serving by virtue of appointment to the House of Lords",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to change the law so that only people elected in a general election or by-election to the House of Commons may serve as government ministers. No person should be able to become a minister solely through appointment to the House of Lords.",
        "closed_at": null,
        "closing_date": "2027-01-23",
